@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' SPEC: _spec/_plans/android-p2p-wiring.puml
' purpose: native Android UI consumes shared domain and P2P contracts
' status: proposed — native UI target supersedes browser-screen wiring
' covers: none — target layout and native wiring are not implemented
' related: _spec/_plans/chess-ui-primitives.puml
' reference: _spec/apps/android/distribution.puml
' reference: _spec/apps/android/webrtc-p2p.puml
 title PLANNED — native Android screens; shared domain and P2P contracts

package "Web composition and proposed native presentation" {
  component "apps/ui\nBrowser screens using packages/ui/web" as WEB <<app>>
  component "apps/ui/android\nNative Android screens" as NATIVE <<app>>
}
component "Shared domain contracts\ncommands · state · capabilities" as DOMAIN <<app>>
component "Native P2P adapter\nhost / join / peer moves" as P2P <<app>>
node "Android service / thin Go host\nsession · tailnet transport" as HOST <<host>>
component "Peer-game capabilities\naiOpponent = false" as CAP <<app>>

WEB ARROW_MAIN DOMAIN : web adapter
NATIVE ARROW_MAIN DOMAIN : native presentation adapter
NATIVE ARROW_MAIN P2P : pair / connect / disconnect
P2P ARROW_MAIN HOST : native service interface
P2P ARROW_MAIN DOMAIN : validated peer commands
DOMAIN ARROW_MAIN CAP : suppress AI reply in peer mode

note bottom of NATIVE
  **Android UIs are expected to be native.**
  Applies to /chess and /starchess alternatives.
  Native screens own pairing and gameplay.
  Browser LanScreen is not the target Android UI.
  A WebView does not satisfy this requirement.
end note

note bottom of WEB
  **Shared web kit: packages/ui/web.**
  apps/ui/android remains a likely native location.
  Native UI shares domain contracts, not web views.
  StarChess directory placement remains open.
  This plan does not relocate source files.
end note

note right of DOMAIN
  Share serializable state / command contracts.
  Native code need not import TypeScript directly.
  Spike runtime / bridge or domain port first.
  Verify equivalent rules with shared fixtures.
  See chess-ui-primitives.puml for analytics.
end note

note right of P2P
  Coach P2P remains this plan's wiring scope.
  Native adapter implements transport contracts.
  P2PClient / window.ChessNative describe the
  earlier browser bridge, not a native UI API.
  StarChess P2P protocol requires a separate plan.
end note

note bottom of HOST
  Keep service and transport responsibilities thin.
  Do not add Maia or Stockfish to the Go host.
  Reassess loopback static UI hosting for native UI.
  Existing distribution specs describe earlier wiring.
  Reconcile them before implementing this target.
end note

legend bottom
  **Implementation order and verification — planned**
  1. Confirm native toolkit, runtime integration and likely web/android layout.
     Reconcile Android distribution and transport specs with native presentation.
  2. Define shared commands, state and native service interfaces.
     Persist contract fixtures for legal moves, results and peer capabilities.
  3. Wire native Coach pairing and gameplay through the native P2P adapter.
     Keep aiOpponent false for human-peer games; prevent duplicate move application.
  4. Validate host/join, move exchange, disconnect/reconnect and service lifecycle
     on Android devices; APK assembly alone does not establish runtime behavior.
  5. Run affected static checks and browser regressions after any directory split.
     Link implementing source and persisted tests when those files exist.
  **Open:** native runtime; final source layout; Headscale vs auth-key provisioning.
  **Scope now:** specification only; no file moves, provisioning or runtime changes.
end legend
@enduml
